Place pre-made EFI authenticated-variable files here so bootc can copy them to
the ESP during installation. systemd-boot offers a one-time enrollment entry
when it finds them in the ESP under loader/keys/auto/.

Expected files (only *.auth files are copied to the ESP):

    PK.auth    — Platform Key     (signed by pk_key, containing pk_cert)
    KEK.auth   — Key Exchange Key (signed by pk_key, containing kek_cert)
    db.auth    — Signature Database (signed by kek_key, containing db_cert)

Regenerate these files with efitools (cert-to-efi-sig-list + sign-efi-sig-list)
whenever the key material changes. The db.auth certificate must match the
db_cert supplied to the build; if they diverge the signed image is unbootable.

This README (and any other non-*.auth file here) is ignored by bootc and is
never copied to the ESP. It exists only to keep the auto/ directory in git. An
auto/ directory with no .auth files means the image ships no enrolment material;
because the build always signs, the image can then only be booted if the
firmware already trusts the build's db certificate.

Do NOT add plain files directly under secureboot-keys/: bootc requires every
entry there to be a directory (each one is a key set), and fails
`bootc install` with "is not a directory" otherwise.
